I have found a solution.  In the defaults file ("defaults.nh" I
believe), you are offered 3 choices for your keyhandler.

The default default is 
OPTIONS=altkeyhandler:nh340key

You can also choose altkeyhandler:nhdefkey  (originally thought as
default default, I guess :-) ).

Both don't work on my XP.

However the third, Ray's keyhandler, does:
OPTIONS=altkeyhandler:nhraykey

(or maybe nhraykey.dll, in any case you just have to remove the comment
from that line and comment out the other one).

Then '\' works just fine.  

I noted that opening a door with a lock pick behaves slightly different
from before (don't know if it is due to the alternative key handler). 
After "applying" "k" (my default slot for lock picks and keys), you
don't immediately get the message "you succeed in picking the lock".
Instead you have to hit return first. 

